{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Extend the 2026 civil limitation reform to cover all forms of childhood abuse",
        "additional_details": "The Crime and Policing Act 2026 removed the civil limitation period for child sexual abuse claims, following IICSA recommendations - but physical and emotional abuse was left out. Survivors of physical and emotional abuse can still be denied the right to bring a civil claim at all, simply because too much time has passed. Scotland removed this barrier for all forms of childhood abuse in 2017. We call on the Government to extend the 2026 reform to physical and emotional abuse too.",
        "background": "The Crime and Policing Act 2026 removed the civil limitation period for child sexual abuse claims in England and Wales. But physical and emotional abuse was left out. Parliament must extend this reform to cover all forms of childhood abuse, as Scotland did in 2017.",
